A large item such as Watermelon, Rabbit or Dumbbells takes the same space as a small item, so you manage inventory by item count and weight instead of shape.

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Existing saves included.[/b] Items already in a save become 1x1 when you load it with the mod installed.[/*]
[*][b]Other inventory limits stay the same.[/b] The mod does not change item weight, stack limits, or container sizes.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx for Survival Log[/url]. Vortex installs it for you.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]Vortex (recommended):[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Click [b]Vortex[/b] at the top of this page [i](needs the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/2471]Survival Log Vortex Extension[/url], which also installs BepInEx)[/i].[/*][/list]

[b]Manual installation:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx[/url].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Survival Log\BepInEx\plugins\CompactInventory.dll[/code][/*][/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
In Vortex, remove the mod on the Mods page. After a manual install, delete [font=Courier New]CompactInventory.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

Before uninstalling, back up your saves (the folder [font=Courier New]%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\LLS\SLGame\Saves[/font]), then spread out or remove items from crowded containers and save. Items regain their normal size on the next load. The game may rearrange items or drop some on the floor beside the container. Check the floor afterward. Making room may help, but is not guaranteed to prevent this.

